app orb-gaps-spec [
  version: "1.0.0",
  description: "Design contract for `orb gaps`. `orb gaps check` reads docs/Almadar_Gaps.md and every repo ledger its roll-up names, and reports duplicate gap codes, repo ledgers without a Next code counter, unreadable ledgers and entries without a [mechanical]/[architectural]/[owner-decision] tag, one line each (status 500, exit 1); a clean tree prints `gaps: clean` (status 200, exit 0). Any other argument list is a usage error (exit 2). `orb gaps sync [--from master|repos] [--write | --check | --out <dir>]` (alias `status` without options) reconciles docs/Almadar_Gaps.md with every active submodule's and explicitly configured foldedLedgers owner's Almadar_Gaps.md (no archive discovery; a declared folded directory participates only when its ledger is present); the exact ownerMoves map relocates master headings and source paths and master/baseline owners before comparison, deprecated owner sections are removed from the active roll-up while their absent baseline entries take the skip path, entries match by gap code, fenced code blocks never count, the three-way merge runs against the baseline file .almadar/gaps-sync-state.json (an edit on one side propagates, identical edits are accepted, divergent edits, edit/delete conflicts, duplicate codes, conflicting owners, a repo named in the roll-up whose ledger is missing, and an unavailable baseline owner stop before any write), a repo's Next code counter never decreases, an absent ledger never closes its gaps. The preview prints one `update|delete master|repo <code>` line per change and `sync: N repo-owned gaps; M ledger files to update[; baseline not initialized]`; --check exits 1 when M is not 0; --write saves the ledger files and the baseline; --out <dir> saves the proposed files and the baseline under the `outRoot` knob's directory (~/.almadar/gaps-out, the program's out grant) in the subdirectory <dir>, a name and not a path, without advancing the live baseline; --from master|repos makes that side authoritative, including deletions. `orb gaps rollup [--write | --check | --out <dir>]` rebuilds Part 2 of the master from the repo ledgers (refusing when the master holds edits sync has not carried) and answers `roll-up: N repo-owned gaps from M repos` (--check: `roll-up current: N repo-owned gaps`, or a stale error, exit 1). `orb gaps plans [--write | --check]` aligns docs/Almadar_Plans.md with docs/Almadar_Gaps.md by root cause: each ledger entry carries exactly one `Root cause: <TAG>.` tag naming a P-017 cause id, one-off or periphery; a cause with no open gaps must be marked [closed] and a [closed] cause must have none; the block between the p017-gaps markers is the generated table (| Cause | Open | Gaps |, causes in Plans order, then one-off and periphery with counts only). The default and --check refuse with one line per problem (exit 1); --write replaces only the block and refuses while any tag or cause problem stands; aligned answers `plans: aligned (N open: ...)`. The working root is the directory the command runs in (the cwd grant anchor); there is no root knob. split is retired."
]

orbital OrbGapsSpec {
  expects trait OrbGaps {
    state ready
    state probing
    state reading
    state scanning
    state analyzing
    state merging
    state updating
    state planning
    state writing
    emits {
      GAPS_ANSWERED { status : number!  body : string! }
    }
  }
  expects page boot -> OrbGaps
}
